        {
          "title": "Multiplication and Division",
          "body": "2.1 Multiplication\nMultiplication is repeated addition and is useful for finding totals of equal groups. Example: 24 boxes\nwith 36 pencils each contain 24 × 36 = 864 pencils.\n\n2.2 Division\nDivision separates a quantity into equal groups. Example: 1,248 books shared equally among 24 classes\ngives 1,248 ÷ 24 = 52 books per class."
        }
